    values:originalText "(2) If the Minister is of the opinion:  (a) that an association represents the interests, in relation to outwards liner cargo shipping services, of all or any of the following kinds of persons:  (i) Australian shippers in a particular trade;  (ii) Australian shippers of particular kinds of goods;  (iii) shippers in a particular part of Australia;  (iv) producers of goods of a kind exported, or proposed to be exported, from Australia; and  (b) that it is desirable that the association be a designated outwards secondary shipper body for the purposes of this Part; the Minister may, by legislative instrument, declare that the association is a designated outwards secondary shipper body for the purposes of this Part." ;
    skos:definition "(2) If the Minister is of the opinion:  (a) that an association represents the interests, in relation to outwards liner cargo shipping services, of all or any of the following kinds of persons:  (i) Australian shippers in a particular trade;  (ii) Australian shippers of particular kinds of goods;  (iii) shippers in a particular part of Australia;  (iv) producers of goods of a kind exported, or proposed to be exported, from Australia; and  (b) that it is desirable that the association be a designated outwards secondary shipper body for the purposes of this Part; the Minister may, by legislative instrument, declare that the association is a designated outwards secondary shipper body for the purposes of this Part."@en ;
