doc:sec-10-112-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "10(2) 04  Application of section 46 in relation to conference agreements" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) In subsection (1): conference agreement means an agreement between members of a conference in relation to international liner cargo shipping services provided, or proposed to be provided, by them, and includes an agreement that varies such an agreement.  Other provisions  Chapter 6 International liner cargo shipping  Part X Minimum standards for conference agreements  Division 3  Section 10.06  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026" ;
    cof:pageNumber "44"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-113 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "10 06  Application of Australian law to outwards conference"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-10-113 ;
    values:originalText "agreements and withdrawal from agreements  (1) An outwards conference agreement must expressly provide for a question arising under the agreement in relation to an outwards liner cargo shipping service provided, or proposed to be provided, under the agreement to be determined in Australia in accordance with Australian law unless the parties and the Minister agree, in writing, to the particular question being otherwise determined.  (2) An outwards conference agreement must expressly permit any party to the agreement to withdraw from the agreement on reasonable notice without penalty." ;
    skos:definition "agreements and withdrawal from agreements  (1) An outwards conference agreement must expressly provide for a question arising under the agreement in relation to an outwards liner cargo shipping service provided, or proposed to be provided, under the agreement to be determined in Australia in accordance with Australian law unless the parties and the Minister agree, in writing, to the particular question being otherwise determined.  (2) An outwards conference agreement must expressly permit any party to the agreement to withdraw from the agreement on reasonable notice without penalty."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b4093b9e2abff35f0885dd658b83aad51b17d692dcad48dec5052703ec39916f" ;
    cof:pageNumber "45"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-113-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-113-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.45" .
doc:sec-10-113 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "10 06  Application of Australian law to outwards conference" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "agreements and withdrawal from agreements  (1) An outwards conference agreement must expressly provide for a question arising under the agreement in relation to an outwards liner cargo shipping service provided, or proposed to be provided, under the agreement to be determined in Australia in accordance with Australian law unless the parties and the Minister agree, in writing, to the particular question being otherwise determined.  (2) An outwards conference agreement must expressly permit any party to the agreement to withdraw from the agreement on reasonable notice without penalty." ;
    cof:pageNumber "45"^^xsd:integer .

