concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-121 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "10 14  Exemptions apply only to certain activities"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-10-121 ;
    values:originalText "(1) Subject to this section, the exemptions provided by this Subdivision apply only in relation to the following parts of an outwards liner cargo shipping service or an inwards liner cargo shipping service:  (a) the parts of the service that consist of the transport of the cargo by sea;  (b) stevedoring services;  (c) activities that take place outside Australia.  (2) The exemptions provided by this Subdivision extend to the fixing of charges for an inter-terminal transport service where the service is part of an outwards liner cargo shipping service or an inwards liner cargo shipping service.  (3) The exemptions provided by this Subdivision extend to the determination of common terms and conditions for bills of lading for use in relation to an outwards liner cargo shipping service or an inwards liner cargo shipping service.  (4) To avoid doubt, the exemptions provided by this Subdivision do not extend to any dealings between the parties to a conference agreement and a person who provides ancillary services on behalf of the provider of a scheduled cargo shipping service." ;
    skos:definition "(1) Subject to this section, the exemptions provided by this Subdivision apply only in relation to the following parts of an outwards liner cargo shipping service or an inwards liner cargo shipping service:  (a) the parts of the service that consist of the transport of the cargo by sea;  (b) stevedoring services;  (c) activities that take place outside Australia.  (2) The exemptions provided by this Subdivision extend to the fixing of charges for an inter-terminal transport service where the service is part of an outwards liner cargo shipping service or an inwards liner cargo shipping service.  (3) The exemptions provided by this Subdivision extend to the determination of common terms and conditions for bills of lading for use in relation to an outwards liner cargo shipping service or an inwards liner cargo shipping service.  (4) To avoid doubt, the exemptions provided by this Subdivision do not extend to any dealings between the parties to a conference agreement and a person who provides ancillary services on behalf of the provider of a scheduled cargo shipping service."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a20071a7df2b00bf222e0e73c9db51ea769a1042c7e09987c8c1f9bdc5702fc4" ;
    cof:pageNumber "50"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-121-ss-1 ;
