concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-122 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "10 15  When do exemptions commence to apply in relation to"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-10-122 ;
    values:originalText "registered conference agreements?  (1) The exemptions provided by this Subdivision (other than sections 10.17A and 10.18A) apply in relation to the operation of a  Other provisions  Chapter 6 International liner cargo shipping  Part X Exemptions from certain restrictive trade practice prohibitions  Division 5  Section 10.16  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  registered outwards conference agreement only after the end of 30 days after the conference agreement is finally registered.  (2) The exemptions provided by this Subdivision (other than sections 10.17A and 10.18A) apply in relation to the operation of a registered inwards conference agreement only after whichever is the later of the following times:  (a) the end of 30 days after the conference agreement is finally registered;  (b) the commencement of Part 2 of Schedule 1 to the Trade Practices Amendment (International Liner Cargo Shipping) Act 2000." ;
    skos:definition "registered conference agreements?  (1) The exemptions provided by this Subdivision (other than sections 10.17A and 10.18A) apply in relation to the operation of a  Other provisions  Chapter 6 International liner cargo shipping  Part X Exemptions from certain restrictive trade practice prohibitions  Division 5  Section 10.16  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  registered outwards conference agreement only after the end of 30 days after the conference agreement is finally registered.  (2) The exemptions provided by this Subdivision (other than sections 10.17A and 10.18A) apply in relation to the operation of a registered inwards conference agreement only after whichever is the later of the following times:  (a) the end of 30 days after the conference agreement is finally registered;  (b) the commencement of Part 2 of Schedule 1 to the Trade Practices Amendment (International Liner Cargo Shipping) Act 2000."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "cb0aee32def195f483ad4f68a1007c359bbfc2d1195305e2a50d2517b34c511e" ;
    cof:pageNumber "50"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-122-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-122-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.50" .
doc:sec-10-122 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "10 15  When do exemptions commence to apply in relation to" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "registered conference agreements?  (1) The exemptions provided by this Subdivision (other than sections 10.17A and 10.18A) apply in relation to the operation of a  Other provisions  Chapter 6 International liner cargo shipping  Part X Exemptions from certain restrictive trade practice prohibitions  Division 5  Section 10.16  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  registered outwards conference agreement only after the end of 30 days after the conference agreement is finally registered.  (2) The exemptions provided by this Subdivision (other than sections 10.17A and 10.18A) apply in relation to the operation of a registered inwards conference agreement only after whichever is the later of the following times:  (a) the end of 30 days after the conference agreement is finally registered;  (b) the commencement of Part 2 of Schedule 1 to the Trade Practices Amendment (International Liner Cargo Shipping) Act 2000." ;
    cof:pageNumber "50"^^xsd:integer .

