concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-125-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "10(4) 17A  Exemptions from sections 45AF, 45AG, 45AJ, 45AK and 45"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-10-125-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) Sections 45AG, 45AK and 45 do not apply to conduct engaged in by a party to a freight rate agreement, so far as the conduct gives effect to freight rate charges in the freight rate agreement, if:  (a) the freight rates (including base freight rates, surcharges, rebates and allowances) specified in the freight rate agreement are for inwards liner cargo shipping services provided under a single registered inwards conference agreement after whichever is the later of the following times:  (i) the end of 30 days after the last-mentioned agreement is finally registered;  (ii) the commencement of Part 2 of Schedule 1 to the Trade Practices Amendment (International Liner Cargo Shipping) Act 2000; and  (b) the parties to the freight rate agreement are the same as the parties to the registered inwards conference agreement." ;
    skos:definition "(4) Sections 45AG, 45AK and 45 do not apply to conduct engaged in by a party to a freight rate agreement, so far as the conduct gives effect to freight rate charges in the freight rate agreement, if:  (a) the freight rates (including base freight rates, surcharges, rebates and allowances) specified in the freight rate agreement are for inwards liner cargo shipping services provided under a single registered inwards conference agreement after whichever is the later of the following times:  (i) the end of 30 days after the last-mentioned agreement is finally registered;  (ii) the commencement of Part 2 of Schedule 1 to the Trade Practices Amendment (International Liner Cargo Shipping) Act 2000; and  (b) the parties to the freight rate agreement are the same as the parties to the registered inwards conference agreement."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "fdb62d497c1d4757d1078b6158c6f318ef4dbf9146052a5d03e9276b34279cbf" ;
