concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-135 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "10 Section 10"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-10-135 ;
    values:originalText "27  Copy of agreement to be filed with application etc.  (1) Subject to subsections (1A) and (1B), an application for the provisional registration of a conference agreement must be accompanied by:  Other provisions  Chapter 6 International liner cargo shipping  Part X Registration of conference agreements  Division 6  Section 10.27A  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (a) a complete copy of the agreement so far as it is in writing (including all provisions of the agreement so far as they are in writing); and  (b) a written memorandum that fully sets out the agreement so far as it is not in writing (including all provisions of the agreement so far as they are not in writing); other than any parts of the agreement that relate to the minimum level of:  (c) in the case of an outwards conference agreement—outwards liner cargo shipping services to be provided under the agreement or an outwards conference agreement that is varied or otherwise affected by the agreement; or  (d) in the case of an inwards conference agreement—inwards liner cargo shipping services to be provided under the agreement or an inwards conference agreement that is varied or otherwise affected by the agreement.  (1A) The copy of the agreement referred to in paragraph (1)(a) need not include the freight rate charges in the agreement.  (1B) The written memorandum referred to in paragraph (1)(b) need not include the freight rate charges in the agreement.  (2) A document that accompanies an application for the provisional registration of a conference agreement must comply with any regulations requiring its verification (in whole or part) by or on behalf of the applicants." ;
    skos:definition "27  Copy of agreement to be filed with application etc.  (1) Subject to subsections (1A) and (1B), an application for the provisional registration of a conference agreement must be accompanied by:  Other provisions  Chapter 6 International liner cargo shipping  Part X Registration of conference agreements  Division 6  Section 10.27A  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (a) a complete copy of the agreement so far as it is in writing (including all provisions of the agreement so far as they are in writing); and  (b) a written memorandum that fully sets out the agreement so far as it is not in writing (including all provisions of the agreement so far as they are not in writing); other than any parts of the agreement that relate to the minimum level of:  (c) in the case of an outwards conference agreement—outwards liner cargo shipping services to be provided under the agreement or an outwards conference agreement that is varied or otherwise affected by the agreement; or  (d) in the case of an inwards conference agreement—inwards liner cargo shipping services to be provided under the agreement or an inwards conference agreement that is varied or otherwise affected by the agreement.  (1A) The copy of the agreement referred to in paragraph (1)(a) need not include the freight rate charges in the agreement.  (1B) The written memorandum referred to in paragraph (1)(b) need not include the freight rate charges in the agreement.  (2) A document that accompanies an application for the provisional registration of a conference agreement must comply with any regulations requiring its verification (in whole or part) by or on behalf of the applicants."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "aeb095c3fa17c398d787f1d47d07dab2b6bd2f5164a27f6f5f04fbde4097753f" ;
    cof:pageNumber "58"^^xsd:integer ;
