concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-140 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "10 31  How application is to be made and verified"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-10-140 ;
    values:originalText "(1) An application for the final registration of a conference agreement must be:  (a) in the appropriate prescribed form;  (b) made to the Registrar in accordance with the regulations; and  (c) accompanied by the appropriate prescribed fee.  (2) The application must comply with any regulations requiring its verification (in whole or part) by or on behalf of the applicants.  (3) The application may be made by a party to the agreement on behalf of the party and other parties to the agreement." ;
    skos:definition "(1) An application for the final registration of a conference agreement must be:  (a) in the appropriate prescribed form;  (b) made to the Registrar in accordance with the regulations; and  (c) accompanied by the appropriate prescribed fee.  (2) The application must comply with any regulations requiring its verification (in whole or part) by or on behalf of the applicants.  (3) The application may be made by a party to the agreement on behalf of the party and other parties to the agreement."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c6ba8b24a532c7a9e4f94021b3f407cc75c407c533756d7008a2cdc37615bf09" ;
    cof:pageNumber "64"^^xsd:integer ;
