concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-10-198 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "10 82B  Functions and powers of Tribunal"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-10-198 ;
    values:originalText "(1) On a review of a decision of the Commission of a kind mentioned in section 10.82A, the Tribunal may make a decision affirming, setting aside or varying the decision of the Commission and, for the purposes of the review, may perform all the functions and exercise all the powers of the Commission.  (2) A decision by the Tribunal affirming, setting aside or varying a decision of the Commission is taken for the purposes of this Act (other than this Division) to be a decision of the Commission.  Other provisions  Chapter 6 International liner cargo shipping  Part X Review of decisions of Commission  Division 14A  Section 10.82C  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (3) For the purposes of a review by the Tribunal, the member of the Tribunal presiding at the review may require the Commission to give such information, make such reports and provide such other assistance to the Tribunal as the member specifies.  (4) For the purposes of a review, the Tribunal may have regard to any information given, documents produced or evidence given to the Commission in connection with the making of the decision to which the review relates. Note: Division 2 of Part IX applies to proceedings before the Tribunal." ;
    skos:definition "(1) On a review of a decision of the Commission of a kind mentioned in section 10.82A, the Tribunal may make a decision affirming, setting aside or varying the decision of the Commission and, for the purposes of the review, may perform all the functions and exercise all the powers of the Commission.  (2) A decision by the Tribunal affirming, setting aside or varying a decision of the Commission is taken for the purposes of this Act (other than this Division) to be a decision of the Commission.  Other provisions  Chapter 6 International liner cargo shipping  Part X Review of decisions of Commission  Division 14A  Section 10.82C  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (3) For the purposes of a review by the Tribunal, the member of the Tribunal presiding at the review may require the Commission to give such information, make such reports and provide such other assistance to the Tribunal as the member specifies.  (4) For the purposes of a review, the Tribunal may have regard to any information given, documents produced or evidence given to the Commission in connection with the making of the decision to which the review relates. Note: Division 2 of Part IX applies to proceedings before the Tribunal."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "969e9060d83e2e1fbef22ca31ae89a10f679b19bc0f33b9d0db2310fac2aa682" ;
    cof:pageNumber "108"^^xsd:integer ;
