concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-131c-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "131C(4) Saving of other laws and remedies"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-131c-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) Except as expressly provided by this Part or the Australian Consumer Law, nothing in this Part or the Australian Consumer Law is taken to limit, restrict or otherwise affect any right or remedy a person would have had if this Part and the Australian Consumer Law had not been enacted.  Other provisions  Chapter 6 Application of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI Application of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Division  Section 131D  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  Subdivision B—Effect of other Commonwealth laws on the Australian Consumer Law" ;
    skos:definition "(4) Except as expressly provided by this Part or the Australian Consumer Law, nothing in this Part or the Australian Consumer Law is taken to limit, restrict or otherwise affect any right or remedy a person would have had if this Part and the Australian Consumer Law had not been enacted.  Other provisions  Chapter 6 Application of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI Application of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Division  Section 131D  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  Subdivision B—Effect of other Commonwealth laws on the Australian Consumer Law"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ace5ea2546e360140e00e3b45f9b93f05c0b07f235f02150a608891d80488964" ;
