concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-132-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "132(3) Commonwealth Minister must issue a proposed ban notice"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-132-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) The proposed ban notice must:  (a) be in writing; and  (b) be published on the internet; and  (c) set out a copy of a draft notice for the imposition of the interim ban or permanent ban; and  (d) set out a summary of the reasons for the proposed imposition of the ban; and  (e) invite any person who supplies, or proposes to supply:  (i) consumer goods of that kind; or  (ii) product related services of that kind;  to notify the Commission, in writing and within a period specified in the notice, if the person wishes the Commission to hold a conference in relation to the proposed imposition of the ban." ;
    skos:definition "(3) The proposed ban notice must:  (a) be in writing; and  (b) be published on the internet; and  (c) set out a copy of a draft notice for the imposition of the interim ban or permanent ban; and  (d) set out a summary of the reasons for the proposed imposition of the ban; and  (e) invite any person who supplies, or proposes to supply:  (i) consumer goods of that kind; or  (ii) product related services of that kind;  to notify the Commission, in writing and within a period specified in the notice, if the person wishes the Commission to hold a conference in relation to the proposed imposition of the ban."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "20ad7e79ae43819549be2708acf1ba09c943e33e53c276b0308050e87d9bb371" ;
