concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-132c a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "132C Notification of conference"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-132c ;
    values:originalText "(1) If one or more persons notify the Commission in accordance with a proposed ban notice, or a proposed recall notice, that they wish the Commission to hold a conference, the Commission must:  (a) appoint a day, time and place for the holding of the conference; and  (b) give written notice to the Commonwealth Minister, and to each person who so notified the Commission, of that day, time and place.  (2) The day appointed must be at least 5 days, but not more than 14 days, after the end of the period:  (a) for a proposed ban notice—specified under paragraph 132(3)(e); or  (b) for a proposed recall notice—specified under paragraph 132A(3)(e).  (3) A notice under paragraph (1)(b) is not a legislative instrument." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If one or more persons notify the Commission in accordance with a proposed ban notice, or a proposed recall notice, that they wish the Commission to hold a conference, the Commission must:  (a) appoint a day, time and place for the holding of the conference; and  (b) give written notice to the Commonwealth Minister, and to each person who so notified the Commission, of that day, time and place.  (2) The day appointed must be at least 5 days, but not more than 14 days, after the end of the period:  (a) for a proposed ban notice—specified under paragraph 132(3)(e); or  (b) for a proposed recall notice—specified under paragraph 132A(3)(e).  (3) A notice under paragraph (1)(b) is not a legislative instrument."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "0ef547cd10ee54ed674ca7467b85f6e40e7b408b3154313f78faae7b922bcf55" ;
    cof:pageNumber "129"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-132c-ss-1 ;
