doc:sec-133-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "133(4) Appointment of inspectors" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) If a direction under subsection (3) is given in writing, the direction is not a legislative instrument." ;
    cof:pageNumber "136"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "133A Identity cards"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-133a ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Chairperson must issue an identity card to a person appointed as an inspector. Form of identity card  (2) The identity card must:  (a) contain the information prescribed by the regulations; and  (b) contain a recent photograph of the person. Offence  (3) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person has been issued with an identity card under subsection (1); and  (b) the person ceases to be an inspector; and  Other provisions  Chapter 6 Application of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI Enforcement  Division 4  Section 133B  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (c) the person does not, as soon as practicable after so ceasing, return the identity card to the Chairperson. Penalty: 1 penalty unit.  (4) An offence against subsection (3) is an offence of strict liability. Note: For strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code. Defence: card lost or destroyed  (5) Subsection (3) does not apply if the identity card was lost or destroyed. Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this subsection: see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code. Inspector must carry card  (6) An inspector issued with an identity card under subsection (1) must carry his or her identity card at all times when exercising powers as an inspector. Subdivision B—Premises to which the public is given access" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Chairperson must issue an identity card to a person appointed as an inspector. Form of identity card  (2) The identity card must:  (a) contain the information prescribed by the regulations; and  (b) contain a recent photograph of the person. Offence  (3) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person has been issued with an identity card under subsection (1); and  (b) the person ceases to be an inspector; and  Other provisions  Chapter 6 Application of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI Enforcement  Division 4  Section 133B  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (c) the person does not, as soon as practicable after so ceasing, return the identity card to the Chairperson. Penalty: 1 penalty unit.  (4) An offence against subsection (3) is an offence of strict liability. Note: For strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code. Defence: card lost or destroyed  (5) Subsection (3) does not apply if the identity card was lost or destroyed. Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this subsection: see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code. Inspector must carry card  (6) An inspector issued with an identity card under subsection (1) must carry his or her identity card at all times when exercising powers as an inspector. Subdivision B—Premises to which the public is given access"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "cdbc39c21ca982950c9881338cbea2069cf9582129b581ee98065af6a4a5af16" ;
    cof:pageNumber "136"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133a-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133a-ss-2 ;
