concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133b a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "133B Power to enter premises to which the public has access—"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-133b ;
    values:originalText "consumer goods  (1) An inspector may enter premises in or from which a person, in trade or commerce, supplies consumer goods, if the public has access to the premises at the time of entry, for the purpose of ascertaining whether:  (a) any of those consumer goods will or may cause injury to any person; or  (b) a reasonably foreseeable use (including a misuse) of those consumer goods will or may cause injury to any person; and remain on the premises for such a purpose while the public has access to the premises.  (2) While on the premises, the inspector may:  Chapter 6  Other provisions" ;
    skos:definition "consumer goods  (1) An inspector may enter premises in or from which a person, in trade or commerce, supplies consumer goods, if the public has access to the premises at the time of entry, for the purpose of ascertaining whether:  (a) any of those consumer goods will or may cause injury to any person; or  (b) a reasonably foreseeable use (including a misuse) of those consumer goods will or may cause injury to any person; and remain on the premises for such a purpose while the public has access to the premises.  (2) While on the premises, the inspector may:  Chapter 6  Other provisions"@en ;
