concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-133h-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "133H(3) Court orders relating to consumer goods that do not comply"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-133h-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) Before making an application under subsection (1), the inspector must:  (a) take reasonable steps to discover who has an interest in the consumer goods; and  (b) if it is practicable to do so, notify each person whom the inspector believes to have such an interest of the proposed application." ;
    skos:definition "(3) Before making an application under subsection (1), the inspector must:  (a) take reasonable steps to discover who has an interest in the consumer goods; and  (b) if it is practicable to do so, notify each person whom the inspector believes to have such an interest of the proposed application."@en ;
