concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "135(3) Inspector may enter premises"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-135-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) However, the inspector is not entitled to enter premises under subsection (1) or (2) unless:  (a) the occupier of the premises has consented to the entry and the inspector has shown his or her identity card if required by the occupier; or  (b) the entry is made under a search warrant; or  (c) the entry is made in circumstances in which the exercise of search-related powers is required without delay in order to protect life or public safety. Note: For requirements relating to the occupier’s consent, see section 135H." ;
    skos:definition "(3) However, the inspector is not entitled to enter premises under subsection (1) or (2) unless:  (a) the occupier of the premises has consented to the entry and the inspector has shown his or her identity card if required by the occupier; or  (b) the entry is made under a search warrant; or  (c) the entry is made in circumstances in which the exercise of search-related powers is required without delay in order to protect life or public safety. Note: For requirements relating to the occupier’s consent, see section 135H."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "7f168246a7e132fd28f83b90ed6fa672717e1cd5acdb67310da6cfa71084348a" ;
