concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135d a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "135D Persons assisting inspectors"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-135d ;
    values:originalText "Inspectors may be assisted by other persons  (1) An inspector may, in entering premises under section 135 and in exercising search-related powers in relation to the premises, be assisted by other persons if that assistance is necessary and reasonable.  (2) A person giving such assistance is a person assisting the inspector. Powers of a person assisting the inspector  (3) A person assisting the inspector may:  (a) enter the premises; and  (b) exercise search-related powers in relation to the premises, but only in accordance with a direction given to the person by the inspector.  Other provisions  Chapter 6 Application of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI Search, seizure and entry  Division 6  Section 135E  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (4) A power exercised by a person assisting the inspector as mentioned in subsection (3) is taken for all purposes to have been exercised by the inspector." ;
    skos:definition "Inspectors may be assisted by other persons  (1) An inspector may, in entering premises under section 135 and in exercising search-related powers in relation to the premises, be assisted by other persons if that assistance is necessary and reasonable.  (2) A person giving such assistance is a person assisting the inspector. Powers of a person assisting the inspector  (3) A person assisting the inspector may:  (a) enter the premises; and  (b) exercise search-related powers in relation to the premises, but only in accordance with a direction given to the person by the inspector.  Other provisions  Chapter 6 Application of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI Search, seizure and entry  Division 6  Section 135E  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (4) A power exercised by a person assisting the inspector as mentioned in subsection (3) is taken for all purposes to have been exercised by the inspector."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "66856edc540bc7beff27d40f88dfc0bb58ad5f467677634e23c89876ed9b16db" ;
    cof:pageNumber "158"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135d-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135d-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135d-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135d-ss-4 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.158" .
doc:sec-135d a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "135D Persons assisting inspectors" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Inspectors may be assisted by other persons  (1) An inspector may, in entering premises under section 135 and in exercising search-related powers in relation to the premises, be assisted by other persons if that assistance is necessary and reasonable.  (2) A person giving such assistance is a person assisting the inspector. Powers of a person assisting the inspector  (3) A person assisting the inspector may:  (a) enter the premises; and  (b) exercise search-related powers in relation to the premises, but only in accordance with a direction given to the person by the inspector.  Other provisions  Chapter 6 Application of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI Search, seizure and entry  Division 6  Section 135E  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (4) A power exercised by a person assisting the inspector as mentioned in subsection (3) is taken for all purposes to have been exercised by the inspector." ;
    cof:pageNumber "158"^^xsd:integer .

