concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135p a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "135P Judge may permit consumer goods or equipment to be"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-135p ;
    values:originalText "retained  (1) An inspector who has seized consumer goods or equipment under a search warrant may, before the end of the period referred to in paragraph 135N(1)(b), apply to a judge of the Federal Court for an order that the inspector may retain the consumer goods or equipment for a further period of up to 60 days.  (2) If:  (a) an application to a judge is made under subsection (1); and  (b) the judge is satisfied that it is necessary in all the circumstances for the inspector to continue to retain the consumer goods or equipment;  Chapter 6  Other provisions" ;
    skos:definition "retained  (1) An inspector who has seized consumer goods or equipment under a search warrant may, before the end of the period referred to in paragraph 135N(1)(b), apply to a judge of the Federal Court for an order that the inspector may retain the consumer goods or equipment for a further period of up to 60 days.  (2) If:  (a) an application to a judge is made under subsection (1); and  (b) the judge is satisfied that it is necessary in all the circumstances for the inspector to continue to retain the consumer goods or equipment;  Chapter 6  Other provisions"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ca67bd59cc4116ac80db5f64cbf4747f26ba929c85e8cc689a6123368d08719b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "163"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135p-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135p-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.163" .
