concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135q a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "135Q Recovery of reasonable costs of seizing consumer goods or"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-135q ;
    values:originalText "equipment  (1) If an inspector seizes consumer goods or equipment under a search warrant:  (a) the person from whom the consumer goods were seized, or the equipment was seized; or  (b) if that person is not entitled to possess the consumer goods or equipment—the owner of the consumer goods or equipment; is liable to pay an amount equal to the costs reasonably incurred by the inspector in seizing the consumer goods or equipment.  (2) An amount payable by a person under subsection (1):  (a) is a debt due by the person to the Commonwealth; and  (b) may be recovered by action in a court of competent jurisdiction." ;
    skos:definition "equipment  (1) If an inspector seizes consumer goods or equipment under a search warrant:  (a) the person from whom the consumer goods were seized, or the equipment was seized; or  (b) if that person is not entitled to possess the consumer goods or equipment—the owner of the consumer goods or equipment; is liable to pay an amount equal to the costs reasonably incurred by the inspector in seizing the consumer goods or equipment.  (2) An amount payable by a person under subsection (1):  (a) is a debt due by the person to the Commonwealth; and  (b) may be recovered by action in a court of competent jurisdiction."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1c09f5a7f47df2ee11dac3abd4010d9b70fb62c46446fd0c872c67a37609a52d" ;
    cof:pageNumber "164"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135q-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135q-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.164" .
doc:sec-135q a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "135Q Recovery of reasonable costs of seizing consumer goods or" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "equipment  (1) If an inspector seizes consumer goods or equipment under a search warrant:  (a) the person from whom the consumer goods were seized, or the equipment was seized; or  (b) if that person is not entitled to possess the consumer goods or equipment—the owner of the consumer goods or equipment; is liable to pay an amount equal to the costs reasonably incurred by the inspector in seizing the consumer goods or equipment.  (2) An amount payable by a person under subsection (1):  (a) is a debt due by the person to the Commonwealth; and  (b) may be recovered by action in a court of competent jurisdiction." ;
    cof:pageNumber "164"^^xsd:integer .

