concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135r a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "135R Destruction or disposal of seized consumer goods or"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-135r ;
    values:originalText "equipment  (1) If:  (a) an inspector seizes consumer goods, or equipment used to supply product-related services, under a search warrant; and  Other provisions  Chapter 6 Application of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI Search, seizure and entry  Division 6  Section 135S  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (b) apart from this section, the inspector is required to return the consumer goods or equipment to a person; and  (c) either:  (i) the inspector cannot, despite making reasonable efforts, locate the person; or  (ii) the person has refused to take possession of the consumer goods or equipment; a court may, on the application of the inspector, make an order authorising the inspector to destroy or otherwise dispose of the consumer goods or equipment.  (2) If subparagraph (1)(c)(ii) applies, the inspector must, before making an application under subsection (1), inform the person referred to in that subparagraph that the inspector proposes to make an application under that subsection.  (3) If:  (a) an order is made under subsection (1); and  (b) subparagraph (1)(c)(ii) applies; the person referred to in that subparagraph is liable to pay an amount equal to the costs reasonably incurred by the inspector in destroying or disposing of the consumer goods or equipment.  (4) An amount payable by a person under subsection (3):  (a) is a debt due by the person to the Commonwealth; and  (b) may be recovered by action in a court of competent jurisdiction. Subdivision E—Embargo notices" ;
    skos:definition "equipment  (1) If:  (a) an inspector seizes consumer goods, or equipment used to supply product-related services, under a search warrant; and  Other provisions  Chapter 6 Application of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI Search, seizure and entry  Division 6  Section 135S  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (b) apart from this section, the inspector is required to return the consumer goods or equipment to a person; and  (c) either:  (i) the inspector cannot, despite making reasonable efforts, locate the person; or  (ii) the person has refused to take possession of the consumer goods or equipment; a court may, on the application of the inspector, make an order authorising the inspector to destroy or otherwise dispose of the consumer goods or equipment.  (2) If subparagraph (1)(c)(ii) applies, the inspector must, before making an application under subsection (1), inform the person referred to in that subparagraph that the inspector proposes to make an application under that subsection.  (3) If:  (a) an order is made under subsection (1); and  (b) subparagraph (1)(c)(ii) applies; the person referred to in that subparagraph is liable to pay an amount equal to the costs reasonably incurred by the inspector in destroying or disposing of the consumer goods or equipment.  (4) An amount payable by a person under subsection (3):  (a) is a debt due by the person to the Commonwealth; and  (b) may be recovered by action in a court of competent jurisdiction. Subdivision E—Embargo notices"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1c09f5a7f47df2ee11dac3abd4010d9b70fb62c46446fd0c872c67a37609a52d" ;
    cof:pageNumber "164"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135r-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-135r-ss-2 ;
