doc:sec-137-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "137(2) Limit on occupational liability" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) However, the professional standards law applies for that purpose:  (a) only in relation to a scheme that was prescribed by the regulations at the time (the contravention time) of the contravention; and  (b) as if the scheme were in force under that law at the contravention time, in the form the scheme would have been in if:  (i) the scheme had not been amended or revoked under that law since the scheme was first prescribed; and  (ii) any additions, omissions, substitutions and other modifications prescribed by the regulations at the contravention time had been made to the scheme. Operation of choice of law rules" ;
    cof:pageNumber "175"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-137-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "137(3) Limit on occupational liability"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-137-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) For the purposes of working out whether a professional standards law of a particular State or Territory applies under subsection (1) in relation to a particular contravention of section 18 of the Australian Consumer Law, choice of law rules operate in relation to the contravention in the same way as they operate in relation to a tort. Professional standards laws" ;
    skos:definition "(3) For the purposes of working out whether a professional standards law of a particular State or Territory applies under subsection (1) in relation to a particular contravention of section 18 of the Australian Consumer Law, choice of law rules operate in relation to the contravention in the same way as they operate in relation to a tort. Professional standards laws"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "cbad8682a8329260ef906f400efc1eb71f91abad56436854f814e48e2dcdc545" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-137 ;
    cof:pageNumber "175"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Professional standards laws apply in relation to contraventions of section 18 of the Australian Consumer Law." ;
