doc:sec-137e-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "137E(1) Limits on compensation orders etc. for death or personal" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A court must not make an order under subsection 237(1) or 238(1) of the Australian Consumer Law to compensate a person for loss or  Other provisions  Chapter 6 Application of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI Remedies  Division 7  Section 137E  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  damage the person suffers because of the conduct of another person to the extent to which:  (a) the action would be based on the conduct contravening a provision of Part 2-1 or 3-1 of the Australian Consumer Law; and  (b) the loss or damage is, or results from, death or personal injury; and  (c) the death or personal injury does not result from smoking or other use of tobacco products." ;
    cof:pageNumber "178"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-137e-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
