concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-137g a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "137G Compliance with orders made under section 137F"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-137g ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) an order made under section 137F applies to the person; and  (b) the person contravenes, or refuses or fails to comply with, the order.  Other provisions  Chapter 6 Application of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI Remedies  Division 7  Section 137H  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—900 penalty units; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—180 penalty units.  (2) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability. Note: For strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) an order made under section 137F applies to the person; and  (b) the person contravenes, or refuses or fails to comply with, the order.  Other provisions  Chapter 6 Application of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI Remedies  Division 7  Section 137H  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—900 penalty units; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—180 penalty units.  (2) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability. Note: For strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "bc3e59dc5cb11e46bebba1b7ab57b37d2ee31aa15b1f8db7d8c2b32b92e94128" ;
    cof:pageNumber "182"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-137g-ss-1 ;
