    cof:title "137G Compliance with orders made under section 137F" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) an order made under section 137F applies to the person; and  (b) the person contravenes, or refuses or fails to comply with, the order.  Other provisions  Chapter 6 Application of the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth  Part XI Remedies  Division 7  Section 137H  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  Penalty:  (a) if the person is a body corporate—900 penalty units; or  (b) if the person is not a body corporate—180 penalty units.  (2) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability. Note: For strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code." ;
    cof:pageNumber "182"^^xsd:integer .

