concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-138a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "138A Conferring jurisdiction on the Federal Circuit and Family"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-138a ;
    values:originalText "Court of Australia (Division 2)  (1) Subject to this section, jurisdiction is conferred on the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2) in relation to any matter arising under this Part or the Australian Consumer Law in respect of which a civil proceeding is instituted by a person other than the Commonwealth Minister.  (2) If proceedings under Part 3-5, or section 236, of the Australian Consumer Law are instituted in, or transferred to, the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2), the Court does not have jurisdiction to award an amount for loss or damage that exceeds:  (a) $750,000; or  (b) if another amount is specified in the regulations—that other amount.  Chapter 6  Other provisions" ;
    skos:definition "Court of Australia (Division 2)  (1) Subject to this section, jurisdiction is conferred on the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2) in relation to any matter arising under this Part or the Australian Consumer Law in respect of which a civil proceeding is instituted by a person other than the Commonwealth Minister.  (2) If proceedings under Part 3-5, or section 236, of the Australian Consumer Law are instituted in, or transferred to, the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2), the Court does not have jurisdiction to award an amount for loss or damage that exceeds:  (a) $750,000; or  (b) if another amount is specified in the regulations—that other amount.  Chapter 6  Other provisions"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4f73cc7aeefa1bef3807fef1e13680564c6f3934be92ce11079c60eb48a46434" ;
    cof:pageNumber "185"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-138a-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-138a-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.185" .
