doc:sec-138c-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "138C(2) Transfer of matters by the Federal Court" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) The Federal Court must not transfer a matter to another court under subsection (1) unless:  (a) the other court has power to grant the remedies sought before the Federal Court in the matter; and  (b) it appears to the Federal Court that:  (i) the matter arises out of, or is related to, a proceeding that is pending in the other court; or  (ii) it is otherwise in the interests of justice that the matter be determined by the other court." ;
    cof:pageNumber "186"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-138c-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "138C(4) Transfer of matters by the Federal Court"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-138c-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) If the Federal Court transfers a matter to another court under subsection (1):  (a) further proceedings in the matter must be as directed by the other court; and  (b) the judgment of the other court in the matter is enforceable throughout Australia and the external Territories as if it were a judgment of the Federal Court." ;
    skos:definition "(4) If the Federal Court transfers a matter to another court under subsection (1):  (a) further proceedings in the matter must be as directed by the other court; and  (b) the judgment of the other court in the matter is enforceable throughout Australia and the external Territories as if it were a judgment of the Federal Court."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f5aafd2386c00bf5b62fadf0458e7cea1e710c62c7219037956f488fa2620f58" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-138c ;
    cof:pageNumber "186"^^xsd:integer ;
