concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-138d a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "138D Transfer of matters by a State or Territory court"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-138d ;
    values:originalText "(1) This section applies if:  (a) a proceeding is pending in a court (other than the Supreme Court) of a State or a Territory; and  (b) a matter for determination in the proceeding arises under this Part or the Australian Consumer Law, other than under Chapter 4 of the Australian Consumer Law.  (2) The court must, if directed to do so by the Federal Court, transfer to the Federal Court:  (a) the matter; and  (b) such other matters for determination in the proceeding, the determination of which would (apart from any law of a State or of the Northern Territory relating to cross-vesting of jurisdiction) be within the jurisdiction of the Federal Court, as the Federal Court determines.  Chapter 6  Other provisions" ;
    skos:definition "(1) This section applies if:  (a) a proceeding is pending in a court (other than the Supreme Court) of a State or a Territory; and  (b) a matter for determination in the proceeding arises under this Part or the Australian Consumer Law, other than under Chapter 4 of the Australian Consumer Law.  (2) The court must, if directed to do so by the Federal Court, transfer to the Federal Court:  (a) the matter; and  (b) such other matters for determination in the proceeding, the determination of which would (apart from any law of a State or of the Northern Territory relating to cross-vesting of jurisdiction) be within the jurisdiction of the Federal Court, as the Federal Court determines.  Chapter 6  Other provisions"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "7febf2ae73eaa074feac9bbb625fff052c9f4a893c74763c1c344a502d8aa5a4" ;
    cof:pageNumber "187"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-138d-ss-1 ;
