    values:originalText "(1) If:  (a) a civil proceeding is pending in the Federal Court; and  (b) a matter for determination in the proceeding arises under this Part or the Australian Consumer Law; the Federal Court may, on the application of a party to the proceeding or of its own motion, transfer the proceeding to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1)." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If:  (a) a civil proceeding is pending in the Federal Court; and  (b) a matter for determination in the proceeding arises under this Part or the Australian Consumer Law; the Federal Court may, on the application of a party to the proceeding or of its own motion, transfer the proceeding to the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 1)."@en ;
