concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-139 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "139 Intervention by the Commission"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-139 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Commission may, with the leave of a court and subject to any conditions imposed by the court, intervene in any proceeding instituted under this Part or the Australian Consumer Law.  (2) If the Commission intervenes in a proceeding, the Commission is taken to be a party to the proceeding and has all the rights, duties and liabilities of such a party." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Commission may, with the leave of a court and subject to any conditions imposed by the court, intervene in any proceeding instituted under this Part or the Australian Consumer Law.  (2) If the Commission intervenes in a proceeding, the Commission is taken to be a party to the proceeding and has all the rights, duties and liabilities of such a party."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b197018f7cbd94d3c2ecf1f4c09897d7e18bf4a16257bc1f00a6c8cfad0d9383" ;
    cof:pageNumber "191"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-139-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-139-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.191" .
