concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-139g a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "139G Regulations"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-139g ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Governor-General may make regulations prescribing matters:  (a) required or permitted by Schedule 2 to be prescribed; or  (b) necessary or convenient to be prescribed for carrying out or giving effect to that Schedule.  (2) Before the Governor-General makes a regulation for the purposes of paragraph 25(n) of Schedule 2 prescribing a kind of term of a contract, or a kind of effect that such a term has, the Commonwealth Minister must take into consideration:  (a) the detriment that a term of that kind would cause to consumers; and  (aa) the detriment that a term of that kind would cause to persons who carry on a business and employ fewer than 100 persons; and  Chapter 6  Other provisions" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Governor-General may make regulations prescribing matters:  (a) required or permitted by Schedule 2 to be prescribed; or  (b) necessary or convenient to be prescribed for carrying out or giving effect to that Schedule.  (2) Before the Governor-General makes a regulation for the purposes of paragraph 25(n) of Schedule 2 prescribing a kind of term of a contract, or a kind of effect that such a term has, the Commonwealth Minister must take into consideration:  (a) the detriment that a term of that kind would cause to consumers; and  (aa) the detriment that a term of that kind would cause to persons who carry on a business and employ fewer than 100 persons; and  Chapter 6  Other provisions"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8550b46387c223a65657e907cb14c466e8fc8aebfbec44ca69d6302e737f8100" ;
    cof:pageNumber "197"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-139g-ss-1 ;
