concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-150k a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "150K Gazettal of jurisdictions that excessively modify the Code"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-150k ;
    values:originalText "(1) If the Minister is satisfied that the laws of a participating jurisdiction have made significant modifications to the Competition Code in its application to persons within the legislative competence of the participating jurisdiction, the Minister may publish a notice in the Gazette stating that the Minister is so satisfied.  (2) The Minister may, by further notice in the Gazette, revoke a notice published under subsection (1).  Chapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If the Minister is satisfied that the laws of a participating jurisdiction have made significant modifications to the Competition Code in its application to persons within the legislative competence of the participating jurisdiction, the Minister may publish a notice in the Gazette stating that the Minister is so satisfied.  (2) The Minister may, by further notice in the Gazette, revoke a notice published under subsection (1).  Chapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6b7102d778db883f295a8c6b15a2a1f5855dcb9361238c98aee310cc4b1ee81a" ;
    cof:pageNumber "213"^^xsd:integer ;
