concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151as a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "151AS Exemption orders"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-151as ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person may apply to the Commission for an order exempting specified conduct of the person from the scope of section 151AJ (which deals with anti-competitive conduct). The order is called an exemption order.  (2) An exemption order is not invalid only because the conduct specified in the order is conduct of a kind that, apart from the order, is outside the scope of section 151AJ (which deals with anti-competitive conduct)." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person may apply to the Commission for an order exempting specified conduct of the person from the scope of section 151AJ (which deals with anti-competitive conduct). The order is called an exemption order.  (2) An exemption order is not invalid only because the conduct specified in the order is conduct of a kind that, apart from the order, is outside the scope of section 151AJ (which deals with anti-competitive conduct)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "429b00672cc9c533846f9efc5a7e18b1eaa3e3d01a32328306336a689dfb9a0f" ;
    cof:pageNumber "233"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151as-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151as-ss-2 ;
