concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151az a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "151AZ Commission may convene conference to discuss application"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-151az ;
    values:originalText "(1) If the Commission receives an application for an exemption order, the Commission may convene a conference to discuss the application.  (2) If the Commission decides to convene a conference, the Commission must give:  (a) the applicant (or a representative of the applicant); and  (b) any other persons whom the Commission considers interested; a reasonable opportunity to attend and take part in the conference.  (3) This Act does not prevent a conference under this section from being combined with a conference under section 90A or 93A if the combined conference relates to the same conduct." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If the Commission receives an application for an exemption order, the Commission may convene a conference to discuss the application.  (2) If the Commission decides to convene a conference, the Commission must give:  (a) the applicant (or a representative of the applicant); and  (b) any other persons whom the Commission considers interested; a reasonable opportunity to attend and take part in the conference.  (3) This Act does not prevent a conference under this section from being combined with a conference under section 90A or 93A if the combined conference relates to the same conduct."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ad0a6e87a6c3a1c55aa43d9a6eb8a7b172840f48161f0a96601d7139ad5c9609" ;
    cof:pageNumber "236"^^xsd:integer ;
