concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151bv a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "151BV Incorrect records"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-151bv ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person must not, in purported compliance with a requirement imposed by the record-keeping rules, make a record of any matter or thing in such a way that it does not correctly record the matter or thing.  (2) A person who contravenes subsection (1) commits an offence punishable on conviction by imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months. Note: See also sections 4AA and 4B of the Crimes Act 1914.  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc.  Chapter 7 The Telecommunications Industry: Anti-competitive conduct and record-keeping rules" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person must not, in purported compliance with a requirement imposed by the record-keeping rules, make a record of any matter or thing in such a way that it does not correctly record the matter or thing.  (2) A person who contravenes subsection (1) commits an offence punishable on conviction by imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months. Note: See also sections 4AA and 4B of the Crimes Act 1914.  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc.  Chapter 7 The Telecommunications Industry: Anti-competitive conduct and record-keeping rules"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "74df4528e26ff68f77fbcfa34cbb30ab0a61f9afb2503a0384ca419ae224e68e" ;
    cof:pageNumber "264"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151bv-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151bv-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.264" .
doc:sec-151bv a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "151BV Incorrect records" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person must not, in purported compliance with a requirement imposed by the record-keeping rules, make a record of any matter or thing in such a way that it does not correctly record the matter or thing.  (2) A person who contravenes subsection (1) commits an offence punishable on conviction by imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months. Note: See also sections 4AA and 4B of the Crimes Act 1914.  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc.  Chapter 7 The Telecommunications Industry: Anti-competitive conduct and record-keeping rules" ;
    cof:pageNumber "264"^^xsd:integer .

