concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151da a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "151DA Authorised conduct—subsection 51(1)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-151da ;
    values:originalText "Objects  (1) The objects of this section are:  (a) to promote the national interest in structural reform of the telecommunications industry; and  (b) to promote uniform national pricing of eligible services supplied by NBN corporations by authorising, for the purposes of subsection 51(1), certain conduct engaged in by NBN corporations. Note 1: If conduct is authorised for the purposes of subsection 51(1), the conduct is disregarded in deciding whether a person has contravened" ;
    skos:definition "Objects  (1) The objects of this section are:  (a) to promote the national interest in structural reform of the telecommunications industry; and  (b) to promote uniform national pricing of eligible services supplied by NBN corporations by authorising, for the purposes of subsection 51(1), certain conduct engaged in by NBN corporations. Note 1: If conduct is authorised for the purposes of subsection 51(1), the conduct is disregarded in deciding whether a person has contravened"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6406805bd9f4f8b5b4f0b09ebe2279b986e96b264858336e7b7d0af9f6f7a10a" ;
    cof:pageNumber "288"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Authorise conduct for promoting national interest and uniform pricing" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.288" ;
    cml:asserts concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-151da-norm .
