concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152ch a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "152CH Ministerial pricing determinations"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-152ch ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make a determination setting out principles dealing with price-related terms and conditions relating to the standard access obligations. The determination is to be known as a Ministerial pricing determination. Note 3A: Subsection 152CBD(2) provides that the Commission must not accept a special access undertaking unless the undertaking is consistent with any Ministerial pricing determination. Note 4: Subsection 152CI(1) provides that a provision of an access undertaking has no effect to the extent that the provision is inconsistent with any Ministerial pricing determination. Note 5: Subsection 152CI(2) provides that a provision of an access determination has no effect to the extent that the provision is inconsistent with any Ministerial pricing determination. Note 5A: Subsection 152CI(3) provides that a provision of binding rules of conduct have no effect to the extent that the provision is inconsistent with any Ministerial pricing determination.  (3) In this section: price-related terms and conditions means terms and conditions relating to price or a method of ascertaining price." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make a determination setting out principles dealing with price-related terms and conditions relating to the standard access obligations. The determination is to be known as a Ministerial pricing determination. Note 3A: Subsection 152CBD(2) provides that the Commission must not accept a special access undertaking unless the undertaking is consistent with any Ministerial pricing determination. Note 4: Subsection 152CI(1) provides that a provision of an access undertaking has no effect to the extent that the provision is inconsistent with any Ministerial pricing determination. Note 5: Subsection 152CI(2) provides that a provision of an access determination has no effect to the extent that the provision is inconsistent with any Ministerial pricing determination. Note 5A: Subsection 152CI(3) provides that a provision of binding rules of conduct have no effect to the extent that the provision is inconsistent with any Ministerial pricing determination.  (3) In this section: price-related terms and conditions means terms and conditions relating to price or a method of ascertaining price."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b211c58c0d05c1ba24618fe171b6f88c8d90be92dafe5f41770f51a76f039d7a" ;
    cof:pageNumber "413"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152ch-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152ch-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.413" .
doc:sec-152ch a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "152CH Ministerial pricing determinations" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make a determination setting out principles dealing with price-related terms and conditions relating to the standard access obligations. The determination is to be known as a Ministerial pricing determination. Note 3A: Subsection 152CBD(2) provides that the Commission must not accept a special access undertaking unless the undertaking is consistent with any Ministerial pricing determination. Note 4: Subsection 152CI(1) provides that a provision of an access undertaking has no effect to the extent that the provision is inconsistent with any Ministerial pricing determination. Note 5: Subsection 152CI(2) provides that a provision of an access determination has no effect to the extent that the provision is inconsistent with any Ministerial pricing determination. Note 5A: Subsection 152CI(3) provides that a provision of binding rules of conduct have no effect to the extent that the provision is inconsistent with any Ministerial pricing determination.  (3) In this section: price-related terms and conditions means terms and conditions relating to price or a method of ascertaining price." ;
    cof:pageNumber "413"^^xsd:integer .

