concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-152ei a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "152EI Interim injunctions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-152ei ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Federal Court may grant an interim injunction pending determination of an application under section 152EG.  (2) If the Commission makes an application under section 152EG to the Federal Court for an injunction, the Court must not require the Commission or any other person, as a condition of granting an interim injunction, to give any undertakings as to damages.  Chapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Federal Court may grant an interim injunction pending determination of an application under section 152EG.  (2) If the Commission makes an application under section 152EG to the Federal Court for an injunction, the Court must not require the Commission or any other person, as a condition of granting an interim injunction, to give any undertakings as to damages.  Chapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a03696878fc0d7af3dbee1afec58690fc125ac3fa1d63de373bac5eff1f6ebd3" ;
    cof:pageNumber "423"^^xsd:integer ;
