    values:originalText "(2) A corporation may be taken to have done something:  (a) for the purpose of substantially lessening competition in an electricity market; or  (b) for the purpose of distorting or manipulating prices in an electricity spot market; even though, after all the evidence has been considered, the existence of that purpose is ascertainable only by inference from the conduct of the corporation or of any other person or from other relevant circumstances." ;
    cof:pageNumber "437"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153k a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "153K Prohibited conduct may be covered by other provisions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-153k ;
    values:originalText "To avoid doubt, this Division does not limit the operation of any other provision of this Act. Example: Particular conduct of a corporation could result in the corporation contravening both section 46 and section 153F.  Chapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc." ;
    skos:definition "To avoid doubt, this Division does not limit the operation of any other provision of this Act. Example: Particular conduct of a corporation could result in the corporation contravening both section 46 and section 153F.  Chapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c359edec35fe51e695fe5d97e98f0a6d8e76930c1e1ada6754d077a837693380" ;
    cof:pageNumber "437"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "No obligation imposed by this section." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.437" ;
