concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153p a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "153P Prohibited conduct notices"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-153p ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Commission may give a corporation a notice (a prohibited conduct notice) in writing, stating one or more recommendations for the kind or kinds of order the Treasurer or the Court could make under Division 5 or 6, if the Commission reasonably believes that:  (a) any of the following conditions are satisfied:  (i) the corporation has engaged in prohibited conduct;  (ii) the corporation is engaging in prohibited conduct; and  (b) the Treasurer or the Court making that kind or those kinds of order in relation to the corporation, or any other connected body corporate in relation to the prohibited conduct, is a proportionate means of preventing the corporation, or any related body corporate, from engaging in that kind of prohibited conduct in the future; and  (c) if that kind of order is, or those kinds of order include, a divestiture order—the following conditions are satisfied:  (i) such a divestiture order will result, or is likely to result, in a benefit to the public;  (ii) if such a divestiture order will result, or is likely to result, in a detriment to the public—the benefit mentioned in subparagraph (i) would, or is likely to, outweigh that detriment.  (2) The notice must:  (a) be expressed to be given under this section; and  (b) state the day on which the notice is given; and  (c) identify:  (i) the corporation; and  Chapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Commission may give a corporation a notice (a prohibited conduct notice) in writing, stating one or more recommendations for the kind or kinds of order the Treasurer or the Court could make under Division 5 or 6, if the Commission reasonably believes that:  (a) any of the following conditions are satisfied:  (i) the corporation has engaged in prohibited conduct;  (ii) the corporation is engaging in prohibited conduct; and  (b) the Treasurer or the Court making that kind or those kinds of order in relation to the corporation, or any other connected body corporate in relation to the prohibited conduct, is a proportionate means of preventing the corporation, or any related body corporate, from engaging in that kind of prohibited conduct in the future; and  (c) if that kind of order is, or those kinds of order include, a divestiture order—the following conditions are satisfied:  (i) such a divestiture order will result, or is likely to result, in a benefit to the public;  (ii) if such a divestiture order will result, or is likely to result, in a detriment to the public—the benefit mentioned in subparagraph (i) would, or is likely to, outweigh that detriment.  (2) The notice must:  (a) be expressed to be given under this section; and  (b) state the day on which the notice is given; and  (c) identify:  (i) the corporation; and  Chapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "26adea895be68618d4263008a29c8bd2ad7a15b412dc43ccbe715f84fbb12499" ;
    cof:pageNumber "441"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153p-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-153p-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.441" .
doc:sec-153p a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "153P Prohibited conduct notices" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Commission may give a corporation a notice (a prohibited conduct notice) in writing, stating one or more recommendations for the kind or kinds of order the Treasurer or the Court could make under Division 5 or 6, if the Commission reasonably believes that:  (a) any of the following conditions are satisfied:  (i) the corporation has engaged in prohibited conduct;  (ii) the corporation is engaging in prohibited conduct; and  (b) the Treasurer or the Court making that kind or those kinds of order in relation to the corporation, or any other connected body corporate in relation to the prohibited conduct, is a proportionate means of preventing the corporation, or any related body corporate, from engaging in that kind of prohibited conduct in the future; and  (c) if that kind of order is, or those kinds of order include, a divestiture order—the following conditions are satisfied:  (i) such a divestiture order will result, or is likely to result, in a benefit to the public;  (ii) if such a divestiture order will result, or is likely to result, in a detriment to the public—the benefit mentioned in subparagraph (i) would, or is likely to, outweigh that detriment.  (2) The notice must:  (a) be expressed to be given under this section; and  (b) state the day on which the notice is given; and  (c) identify:  (i) the corporation; and  Chapter 7  Further provisions relating to particular industries etc." ;
    cof:pageNumber "441"^^xsd:integer .

