concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154c a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "154C Identity cards"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-154c ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Chairperson must issue an identity card to an inspector. Form of identity card  (2) The identity card must:  (a) contain the information prescribed by the regulations; and  (b) contain a recent photograph of the inspector. Offence  (3) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person has been issued with an identity card; and  (b) the person ceases to be an inspector; and  (c) the person does not return the identity card to the Chairperson as soon as practicable. Penalty: 1 penalty unit.  Miscellaneous  Chapter 8 Search and seizure  Part XID Appointment of inspectors and identity cards  Division 2  Section 154C  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (4) An offence against subsection (3) is an offence of strict liability. Note: For strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code. Card lost or destroyed  (5) Subsection (3) does not apply if the identity card was lost or destroyed. Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this subsection: see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code. Inspector must carry card  (6) An inspector must carry his or her identity card at all times when exercising powers or performing functions as an inspector. Inspector must produce card on request  (7) An inspector is not entitled to exercise any powers under this Part in relation to premises if:  (a) the occupier of the premises has requested the inspector to produce the inspector’s identity card for inspection by the occupier; and  (b) the inspector fails to comply with the request.  Chapter 8  Miscellaneous" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Chairperson must issue an identity card to an inspector. Form of identity card  (2) The identity card must:  (a) contain the information prescribed by the regulations; and  (b) contain a recent photograph of the inspector. Offence  (3) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person has been issued with an identity card; and  (b) the person ceases to be an inspector; and  (c) the person does not return the identity card to the Chairperson as soon as practicable. Penalty: 1 penalty unit.  Miscellaneous  Chapter 8 Search and seizure  Part XID Appointment of inspectors and identity cards  Division 2  Section 154C  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (4) An offence against subsection (3) is an offence of strict liability. Note: For strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code. Card lost or destroyed  (5) Subsection (3) does not apply if the identity card was lost or destroyed. Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in this subsection: see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code. Inspector must carry card  (6) An inspector must carry his or her identity card at all times when exercising powers or performing functions as an inspector. Inspector must produce card on request  (7) An inspector is not entitled to exercise any powers under this Part in relation to premises if:  (a) the occupier of the premises has requested the inspector to produce the inspector’s identity card for inspection by the occupier; and  (b) the inspector fails to comply with the request.  Chapter 8  Miscellaneous"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5f45c62e18d92cad6a65728b69cf1d7d8bbc53d6a08efe9b61443b487ca4d333" ;
    cof:pageNumber "494"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154c-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154c-ss-2 ;
