    skos:definition "(1) A search warrant that is in force in relation to premises authorises the executing officer or an officer assisting to do any of the following:  (a) enter the premises;  (b) search the premises, and any thing on the premises, for the kind of evidential material specified in the warrant, and seize things of that kind found on the premises;  (c) make copies of the kind of evidential material specified in the warrant found on the premises;  (d) operate electronic equipment at the premises to see whether the kind of evidential material specified in the warrant is accessible by doing so (including evidential material not held at the premises); Note: See also Division 5 (which contains provisions relating to the operation of electronic equipment at the premises).  (e) take equipment and material onto the premises, and use it, for any of the above purposes."@en ;
