concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154j a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "154J Securing electronic equipment for use by experts"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-154j ;
    values:originalText "(1) If a search warrant in relation to premises is being executed and the executing officer or an officer assisting believes on reasonable grounds that:  (a) the kind of evidential material specified in the warrant may be accessible by operating electronic equipment at the premises; and  (b) expert assistance is required to operate the equipment; and  (c) if he or she does not take action under this subsection, the material may be destroyed, altered or otherwise interfered with; he or she may do whatever is necessary to secure the equipment, whether by locking it up, placing a guard or otherwise. Notice to occupier  (2) The executing officer or officer assisting must give notice to the occupier of the premises of his or her intention to secure the equipment and of the fact that the equipment may be secured for up to 24 hours. Period equipment may be secured  (3) The equipment may be secured:  (a) for a period not exceeding 24 hours; or  (b) until the equipment has been operated by the expert; whichever happens first.  Chapter 8  Miscellaneous" ;
    skos:definition "(1) If a search warrant in relation to premises is being executed and the executing officer or an officer assisting believes on reasonable grounds that:  (a) the kind of evidential material specified in the warrant may be accessible by operating electronic equipment at the premises; and  (b) expert assistance is required to operate the equipment; and  (c) if he or she does not take action under this subsection, the material may be destroyed, altered or otherwise interfered with; he or she may do whatever is necessary to secure the equipment, whether by locking it up, placing a guard or otherwise. Notice to occupier  (2) The executing officer or officer assisting must give notice to the occupier of the premises of his or her intention to secure the equipment and of the fact that the equipment may be secured for up to 24 hours. Period equipment may be secured  (3) The equipment may be secured:  (a) for a period not exceeding 24 hours; or  (b) until the equipment has been operated by the expert; whichever happens first.  Chapter 8  Miscellaneous"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "39d7956e7c480ace3c5ba2edfc434a333a8948baf4443f08fde1351be5d48df0" ;
    cof:pageNumber "503"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154j-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154j-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154j-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.503" .
doc:sec-154j a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "154J Securing electronic equipment for use by experts" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) If a search warrant in relation to premises is being executed and the executing officer or an officer assisting believes on reasonable grounds that:  (a) the kind of evidential material specified in the warrant may be accessible by operating electronic equipment at the premises; and  (b) expert assistance is required to operate the equipment; and  (c) if he or she does not take action under this subsection, the material may be destroyed, altered or otherwise interfered with; he or she may do whatever is necessary to secure the equipment, whether by locking it up, placing a guard or otherwise. Notice to occupier  (2) The executing officer or officer assisting must give notice to the occupier of the premises of his or her intention to secure the equipment and of the fact that the equipment may be secured for up to 24 hours. Period equipment may be secured  (3) The equipment may be secured:  (a) for a period not exceeding 24 hours; or  (b) until the equipment has been operated by the expert; whichever happens first.  Chapter 8  Miscellaneous" ;
    cof:pageNumber "503"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154j-ss-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "154J(1) Securing electronic equipment for use by experts"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-154j-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If a search warrant in relation to premises is being executed and the executing officer or an officer assisting believes on reasonable grounds that:  (a) the kind of evidential material specified in the warrant may be accessible by operating electronic equipment at the premises; and  (b) expert assistance is required to operate the equipment; and  (c) if he or she does not take action under this subsection, the material may be destroyed, altered or otherwise interfered with; he or she may do whatever is necessary to secure the equipment, whether by locking it up, placing a guard or otherwise. Notice to occupier" ;
    skos:definition "(1) If a search warrant in relation to premises is being executed and the executing officer or an officer assisting believes on reasonable grounds that:  (a) the kind of evidential material specified in the warrant may be accessible by operating electronic equipment at the premises; and  (b) expert assistance is required to operate the equipment; and  (c) if he or she does not take action under this subsection, the material may be destroyed, altered or otherwise interfered with; he or she may do whatever is necessary to secure the equipment, whether by locking it up, placing a guard or otherwise. Notice to occupier"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d3f9698febf7d7d3b1e9de595e03c72fe74b1cda608bcb5c9a563be2f767b05a" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154j ;
    cof:pageNumber "503"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Executing officer must secure electronic equipment if necessary to prevent destruction or alteration of evidence." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
