doc:sec-154k a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "154K Authorisation of officers assisting" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "The executing officer for a search warrant may, by writing, authorise a member of the Australian Federal Police, a member of the staff assisting the Commission, or a consultant, to assist in executing the warrant." ;
    cof:pageNumber "504"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154l a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "154L Availability of assistance and use of force in executing a search"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-154l ;
    values:originalText "warrant  In executing a search warrant:  (a) the executing officer may obtain such assistance as is necessary and reasonable in the circumstances; and  (b) the executing officer, or another inspector who is an officer assisting, may use such force against persons and things as is necessary and reasonable in the circumstances; and  (ba) a member of the Australian Federal Police who is an officer assisting may use such force against persons and things as is necessary and reasonable in the circumstances; and  Miscellaneous  Chapter 8 Search and seizure  Part XID Entry to premises under a search warrant  Division 4  Section 154M  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (c) a person who is not an inspector, but who is an officer assisting, may use such force against things as is necessary and reasonable in the circumstances. Subdivision C—Obligations of executing officer and officers assisting" ;
    skos:definition "warrant  In executing a search warrant:  (a) the executing officer may obtain such assistance as is necessary and reasonable in the circumstances; and  (b) the executing officer, or another inspector who is an officer assisting, may use such force against persons and things as is necessary and reasonable in the circumstances; and  (ba) a member of the Australian Federal Police who is an officer assisting may use such force against persons and things as is necessary and reasonable in the circumstances; and  Miscellaneous  Chapter 8 Search and seizure  Part XID Entry to premises under a search warrant  Division 4  Section 154M  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (c) a person who is not an inspector, but who is an officer assisting, may use such force against things as is necessary and reasonable in the circumstances. Subdivision C—Obligations of executing officer and officers assisting"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e778ecea7a97f84403872e450d20c51df0f8cd2bfdebf1dc159aaff07ff3f47b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "504"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Executing officer may obtain assistance and use force as necessary and reasonable in circumstances." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
