doc:sec-154l a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "154L Availability of assistance and use of force in executing a search" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "warrant  In executing a search warrant:  (a) the executing officer may obtain such assistance as is necessary and reasonable in the circumstances; and  (b) the executing officer, or another inspector who is an officer assisting, may use such force against persons and things as is necessary and reasonable in the circumstances; and  (ba) a member of the Australian Federal Police who is an officer assisting may use such force against persons and things as is necessary and reasonable in the circumstances; and  Miscellaneous  Chapter 8 Search and seizure  Part XID Entry to premises under a search warrant  Division 4  Section 154M  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (c) a person who is not an inspector, but who is an officer assisting, may use such force against things as is necessary and reasonable in the circumstances. Subdivision C—Obligations of executing officer and officers assisting" ;
    cof:pageNumber "504"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154m a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "154M Announcement before entry"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-154m ;
    values:originalText "(1) Before any person enters premises under a search warrant, the executing officer must:  (a) announce that he or she is authorised to enter the premises; and  (b) give any person at the premises an opportunity to allow entry to the premises.  (2) However, the executing officer is not required to comply with subsection (1) if he or she believes on reasonable grounds that immediate entry to the premises is required to ensure that the effective execution of the warrant is not frustrated." ;
    skos:definition "(1) Before any person enters premises under a search warrant, the executing officer must:  (a) announce that he or she is authorised to enter the premises; and  (b) give any person at the premises an opportunity to allow entry to the premises.  (2) However, the executing officer is not required to comply with subsection (1) if he or she believes on reasonable grounds that immediate entry to the premises is required to ensure that the effective execution of the warrant is not frustrated."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "94387bcb44c0e610050819f08fe3378e623bb3e83bd4c35d77edf1370d0d02e7" ;
    cof:pageNumber "505"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154m-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154m-ss-2 ;
