    skos:prefLabel "154Z(2) Offences relating to warrants"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-154z-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) An inspector must not:  (a) state in a document that purports to be a form of warrant under section 154Y the name of a magistrate unless that magistrate issued the warrant; or  (b) state on a form of warrant under that section a matter that, to the inspector’s knowledge, departs in a material particular from the form authorised by the magistrate; or  (c) purport to execute, or present to another person, a document that purports to be a form of warrant under that section that the inspector knows:  (i) has not been approved by a magistrate under that section; or  (ii) departs in a material particular from the terms authorised by a magistrate under that section; or  (d) give to a magistrate a form of warrant under that section that is not the form of warrant that the inspector purported to execute. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.  Miscellaneous  Chapter 8 Search and seizure  Part XID Entry to premises under a search warrant  Division 4  Section 154ZA  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  Subdivision G—Powers of magistrates" ;
    skos:definition "(2) An inspector must not:  (a) state in a document that purports to be a form of warrant under section 154Y the name of a magistrate unless that magistrate issued the warrant; or  (b) state on a form of warrant under that section a matter that, to the inspector’s knowledge, departs in a material particular from the form authorised by the magistrate; or  (c) purport to execute, or present to another person, a document that purports to be a form of warrant under that section that the inspector knows:  (i) has not been approved by a magistrate under that section; or  (ii) departs in a material particular from the terms authorised by a magistrate under that section; or  (d) give to a magistrate a form of warrant under that section that is not the form of warrant that the inspector purported to execute. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.  Miscellaneous  Chapter 8 Search and seizure  Part XID Entry to premises under a search warrant  Division 4  Section 154ZA  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  Subdivision G—Powers of magistrates"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "78e708c3a5f08c03616c6eac94f7457869b78bb028544bab678599296bac7db6" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154z ;
    cof:pageNumber "514"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Inspection must not state or purport certain information about warrants." ;
