    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sec-154zb a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "154ZB Operation of electronic equipment at premises" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "A person may operate electronic equipment at premises in order to exercise a power under this Part only if he or she believes on reasonable grounds that the operation of the equipment can be carried out without damage to the equipment." ;
    cof:pageNumber "516"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zc a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "154ZC Compensation for damage to electronic equipment"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-154zc ;
    values:originalText "(1) This section applies if:  (a) as a result of electronic equipment being operated as mentioned in section 154E, 154F, 154G, 154H or 154J:  (i) damage is caused to the equipment; or  (ii) the data recorded on the equipment is damaged; or  (iii) programs associated with the use of the equipment, or with the use of the data, are damaged or corrupted; and  (b) the damage or corruption occurs because:  (i) insufficient care was exercised in selecting the person who was to operate the equipment; or  (ii) insufficient care was exercised by the person operating the equipment.  (2) The Commonwealth must pay the owner of the equipment, or the user of the data or programs, such reasonable compensation for the damage or corruption as the Commonwealth and the owner or user agree on.  (3) However, if the owner or user and the Commonwealth fail to agree, the owner or user may institute proceedings in the Federal Court of Australia for such reasonable amount of compensation as the Court determines.  Miscellaneous  Chapter 8 Search and seizure  Part XID General provisions relating to electronic equipment  Division 5  Section 154ZC  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (4) In determining the amount of compensation payable, regard is to be had to whether the occupier of the premises, or the occupier’s employees and agents, if they were available at the time, provided any appropriate warning or guidance on the operation of the equipment.  (5) Compensation is payable out of money appropriated by the Parliament.  (6) For the purposes of subsection (1): damage, in relation to data, includes damage by erasure of data or addition of other data.  Chapter 8  Miscellaneous" ;
    skos:definition "(1) This section applies if:  (a) as a result of electronic equipment being operated as mentioned in section 154E, 154F, 154G, 154H or 154J:  (i) damage is caused to the equipment; or  (ii) the data recorded on the equipment is damaged; or  (iii) programs associated with the use of the equipment, or with the use of the data, are damaged or corrupted; and  (b) the damage or corruption occurs because:  (i) insufficient care was exercised in selecting the person who was to operate the equipment; or  (ii) insufficient care was exercised by the person operating the equipment.  (2) The Commonwealth must pay the owner of the equipment, or the user of the data or programs, such reasonable compensation for the damage or corruption as the Commonwealth and the owner or user agree on.  (3) However, if the owner or user and the Commonwealth fail to agree, the owner or user may institute proceedings in the Federal Court of Australia for such reasonable amount of compensation as the Court determines.  Miscellaneous  Chapter 8 Search and seizure  Part XID General provisions relating to electronic equipment  Division 5  Section 154ZC  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (4) In determining the amount of compensation payable, regard is to be had to whether the occupier of the premises, or the occupier’s employees and agents, if they were available at the time, provided any appropriate warning or guidance on the operation of the equipment.  (5) Compensation is payable out of money appropriated by the Parliament.  (6) For the purposes of subsection (1): damage, in relation to data, includes damage by erasure of data or addition of other data.  Chapter 8  Miscellaneous"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "aa46e0afac51d9fa8dc82310146ab30092035277c12821763e989e654be15e70" ;
    cof:pageNumber "516"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zc-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zc-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zc-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zc-ss-4 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zc-ss-5 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-154zc-ss-6 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.516" .
doc:sec-154zc a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "154ZC Compensation for damage to electronic equipment" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) This section applies if:  (a) as a result of electronic equipment being operated as mentioned in section 154E, 154F, 154G, 154H or 154J:  (i) damage is caused to the equipment; or  (ii) the data recorded on the equipment is damaged; or  (iii) programs associated with the use of the equipment, or with the use of the data, are damaged or corrupted; and  (b) the damage or corruption occurs because:  (i) insufficient care was exercised in selecting the person who was to operate the equipment; or  (ii) insufficient care was exercised by the person operating the equipment.  (2) The Commonwealth must pay the owner of the equipment, or the user of the data or programs, such reasonable compensation for the damage or corruption as the Commonwealth and the owner or user agree on.  (3) However, if the owner or user and the Commonwealth fail to agree, the owner or user may institute proceedings in the Federal Court of Australia for such reasonable amount of compensation as the Court determines.  Miscellaneous  Chapter 8 Search and seizure  Part XID General provisions relating to electronic equipment  Division 5  Section 154ZC  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (4) In determining the amount of compensation payable, regard is to be had to whether the occupier of the premises, or the occupier’s employees and agents, if they were available at the time, provided any appropriate warning or guidance on the operation of the equipment.  (5) Compensation is payable out of money appropriated by the Parliament.  (6) For the purposes of subsection (1): damage, in relation to data, includes damage by erasure of data or addition of other data.  Chapter 8  Miscellaneous" ;
    cof:pageNumber "516"^^xsd:integer .

