    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) If the Minister:  (a) decides to vary or revoke a designated complainant’s approval; or  (b) in a case where a designated complainant has applied for a variation or revocation of its approval—decides not to vary or revoke the approval; the Minister must give the designated complainant, as soon as practicable:  (c) notice of the decision; and  (d) if the decision is to vary or revoke the approval—a copy of the variation or revocation." ;
