doc:sec-155b-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "155B(3) Australian Competition and Consumer Commission may" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) A person must not:  Miscellaneous  Chapter 8 Miscellaneous  Part XII  Section 155B  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (a) contravene a notice under section 98H of the Commerce Act 1986 of New Zealand; or  (b) in purported compliance with such a notice, knowingly furnish information that is false or misleading in a material particular. Penalty: 20 penalty units. Note 1: Chapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of criminal responsibility. Note 2: Part IA of the Crimes Act 1914 contains provisions dealing with penalties." ;
    cof:pageNumber "550"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-155b-ss-3a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "155B(3A) Australian Competition and Consumer Commission may"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-155b-ss-3a ;
    values:originalText "(3A) Paragraph (3)(a) does not apply if the person has a reasonable excuse. Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matters in subsection (3A), see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code." ;
    skos:definition "(3A) Paragraph (3)(a) does not apply if the person has a reasonable excuse. Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matters in subsection (3A), see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code."@en ;
