concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-157aa-ss-2a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "157AA(2A) Disclosure of CDR-related information by Commission"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-157aa-ss-2a ;
    values:originalText "(2A) The Commission or a Commission official may disclose to:  (a) the Secretary of the Department; or  (b) any employee of the Department or consultant assisting the Secretary in performing the Secretary’s functions, or exercising the Secretary’s powers, relating to Part IVD; any information that the Commission obtains under this Act, or the consumer data rules, that is relevant or likely to be relevant to the functions or powers referred to in paragraph (b). Note: The Privacy Act 1988 also contains provisions relevant to the use and disclosure of information." ;
    skos:definition "(2A) The Commission or a Commission official may disclose to:  (a) the Secretary of the Department; or  (b) any employee of the Department or consultant assisting the Secretary in performing the Secretary’s functions, or exercising the Secretary’s powers, relating to Part IVD; any information that the Commission obtains under this Act, or the consumer data rules, that is relevant or likely to be relevant to the functions or powers referred to in paragraph (b). Note: The Privacy Act 1988 also contains provisions relevant to the use and disclosure of information."@en ;
