doc:sec-157d-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "157D(3) General powers of a court" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) A refusal by a court to grant leave under subsection 157B(1) does not prevent the court from later ordering that a civil proceeding be stayed on the ground that the refusal would have a substantial adverse effect on the hearing in the proceeding." ;
    cof:pageNumber "564"^^xsd:integer .

concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-157d-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "157D(4) General powers of a court"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-157d-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) In deciding whether to order a stay of the civil proceeding, the court must consider:  Miscellaneous  Chapter 8 Miscellaneous  Part XII  Section 158  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (a) the extent of any financial loss that a party would suffer as a result of the proceeding being stayed; and  (b) whether a party has reasonable prospects of obtaining a remedy in the proceeding; and  (c) any other matter the court considers relevant." ;
    skos:definition "(4) In deciding whether to order a stay of the civil proceeding, the court must consider:  Miscellaneous  Chapter 8 Miscellaneous  Part XII  Section 158  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (a) the extent of any financial loss that a party would suffer as a result of the proceeding being stayed; and  (b) whether a party has reasonable prospects of obtaining a remedy in the proceeding; and  (c) any other matter the court considers relevant."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f6c30792df0ad9dce70c55cbbe72f40b57a281d0575df33cedf18bb2dcd038a4" ;
    values:partOf concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-157d ;
    cof:pageNumber "564"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Court must consider certain factors when deciding to order a stay of civil proceeding." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
