concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-159 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "159 Incriminating answers"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-159 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person appearing before the Commission to give evidence or produce documents is not excused from answering a question, or producing a document, on the ground that the answer to the question, or the document, may tend to incriminate the person or expose the person to a penalty.  (2) Evidence given by an individual before the Commission is not admissible against the individual in any criminal proceedings, other than:  (a) proceedings for an offence against this Part; or  Miscellaneous  Chapter 8 Miscellaneous  Part XII  Section 160  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (b) proceedings for an offence against section 137.1, 137.2 or" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person appearing before the Commission to give evidence or produce documents is not excused from answering a question, or producing a document, on the ground that the answer to the question, or the document, may tend to incriminate the person or expose the person to a penalty.  (2) Evidence given by an individual before the Commission is not admissible against the individual in any criminal proceedings, other than:  (a) proceedings for an offence against this Part; or  Miscellaneous  Chapter 8 Miscellaneous  Part XII  Section 160  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  (b) proceedings for an offence against section 137.1, 137.2 or"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "619beb576f291b8bfd7a771b6091750d9d01bce5f64582ebe090b9e82a5a6aa3" ;
    cof:pageNumber "568"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-159-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-159-ss-2 ;
