concept:competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sec-162 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "162 Contempt"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-162 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person shall not:  (a) insult a member of the Tribunal, a member of the Commission or an AER member in the exercise of his or her powers or functions as a member;  (b) interrupt the proceedings of the Tribunal or a conference held by the Commission under section 90 or 93A, Division 3 of Part XI or section 151AZ;  (c) create a disturbance, or take part in creating or continuing a disturbance, in or near a place where the Tribunal is sitting or the Commission is holding such a conference; or  (d) do any other act or thing that would, if the Tribunal were a court of record, constitute a contempt of that court.  (2) A person who contravenes subsection (1) is guilty of an offence punishable on conviction by a fine not exceeding 20 penalty units or imprisonment for 12 months. Note 1: Chapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of criminal responsibility.  Miscellaneous  Chapter 8 Miscellaneous  Part XII  Section 162A  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  Note 2: Part IA of the Crimes Act 1914 contains provisions dealing with penalties." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person shall not:  (a) insult a member of the Tribunal, a member of the Commission or an AER member in the exercise of his or her powers or functions as a member;  (b) interrupt the proceedings of the Tribunal or a conference held by the Commission under section 90 or 93A, Division 3 of Part XI or section 151AZ;  (c) create a disturbance, or take part in creating or continuing a disturbance, in or near a place where the Tribunal is sitting or the Commission is holding such a conference; or  (d) do any other act or thing that would, if the Tribunal were a court of record, constitute a contempt of that court.  (2) A person who contravenes subsection (1) is guilty of an offence punishable on conviction by a fine not exceeding 20 penalty units or imprisonment for 12 months. Note 1: Chapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of criminal responsibility.  Miscellaneous  Chapter 8 Miscellaneous  Part XII  Section 162A  Competition and Consumer Act 2010  Compilation date: 27/05/2026  Note 2: Part IA of the Crimes Act 1914 contains provisions dealing with penalties."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "73dba637276ae9b96b06b7e83a0bb8cbe554c29d1cadbdcd26bfd69ff0fe68fe" ;
